# The image needs only package.json, bun.lock and src/ (see Dockerfile).
# Everything else stays out of the build context: smaller uploads, no secrets, no databases.
# Patterns without **/ match at the repository root only (e.g. `data` is not `src/data`).

# Dependencies and build output
**/node_modules
**/dist
out
coverage
*.tgz
*.lcov

# VCS and CI
.git
.github

# Databases, backups and rollback copies (never bake data into an image). Keep these patterns
# specific: drizzle-kit names migrations <n>_<word>_<word>.sql from word lists that include
# "old", so a loose pattern such as **/*_old* could silently drop a migration from the image.
# tests/modules/ops checks that nothing under src/ is excluded.
**/sqlite.db*
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.bak
data
config

# Secrets
.env*

# Not needed at runtime
tests
docs
scripts
README.md
compose.yaml
compose.dev.yaml
fly.toml
drizzle.config.ts
tsconfig.json
.oxlintrc.json
.oxfmtrc.json

# Logs, caches and editor files
logs
*.log
.cache
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
